    "title": "The Netherlands' first wave of online licences starts expiring on 1 October",
    "meta": "SBC News | 10 Aug 2026",
    "summary": "The five-year licences issued when the Netherlands re-regulated in October 2021 begin expiring on 1 October 2026. Holland Casino, Bingoal and Nederlandse Loterij's TOTO Online have confirmed five-year extensions from that date after KSA review, but Entain's BetCity (third by market share), bet365 (fourth), Play North's Kansino (ninth) and Janshen-Hahnraths' Fair Play (tenth) are all still awaiting renewal. JVH's Jacks.nl expires on 20 November, while Unibet, 711, OneCasino and ComeOn have runways into 2027.",
    "why": "Licence renewal is the moment a regulator can reprice its relationship with every incumbent at once, and the Dutch market has changed beyond recognition since 2021 — from 10 licensees to more than 30, with an advertising ban, a sponsorship ban and tax at 37.8% layered on top. For anyone supplying or operating in the market, the practical question is not whether renewals are granted but what conditions ride along with them.",
    "expanded": "BetCity's position is the one to watch: it has repeatedly clashed with the KSA over marketing, admitting a young-adult advertising breach in March 2026 and being contacted again over the use of role models during the World Cup. VNLOK puts the black market at roughly 25% of 2025 Dutch activity while the KSA says the legal market's GGR share fell to about 49% early last year — which makes voluntary exit a live commercial option for smaller licensees rather than a theoretical one, and a genuine churn risk for platform providers with Dutch-only integrations.",
