    "title": "Meloni drops Italy's land-based reorganisation decree and extends retail concessions another year",
    "meta": "SBC News | 6 Aug 2026",
    "summary": "Prime Minister Giorgia Meloni has removed the land-based gambling 'Reorganisation Decree' from Italy's remaining 2026 political agenda, omitting it from the Council of Ministers policy plan and ending nearly two years of negotiation between the state, autonomous regions and municipalities. Government sources say she was dissatisfied that the settlement still left significant power over venue distances, opening hours and licensing conditions with regional and municipal authorities rather than delivering uniform governance under ADM. The MEF and ADM will keep enforcing existing retail betting, gaming machine and bingo concessions for a further 12 months.",
    "why": "Italy's retail estate has been waiting on this decree to unlock a consolidation cycle, and another year of extended concessions means another year in which nobody can price a retail asset properly. That uncertainty bleeds into the online side too, since the same groups fund digital investment out of retail cash flow.",
    "expanded": "The fiscal backdrop makes the delay harder to justify: MEF figures show total gaming tax revenues fell 6.3% year-on-year to €3.64bn in H1 2026, indirect receipts from lotteries and other gaming dropped 8.4% to €3.07bn, and gaming machine tax receipts fell 7.3% to €2.47bn. Lottomatica chairman and CEO Guglielmo Angelozzi was blunt with investors about the practical effect: \"Whether you have an agreement or not, basically nothing changes. The outcome is exactly the same in the next two to three years.\"",
