    "title": "ADM orders Italian ISPs to block 190 more unlicensed gambling domains by 20 August",
    "meta": "European Gaming | 10 Aug 2026",
    "summary": "Italy's Agenzia delle Dogane e dei Monopoli ordered the blocking of 190 new gambling domains in a note registered on 5 August 2026 under protocol 00540333, signed by Gambling Controls Office manager Luca Turchi. Connectivity providers have an absolute deadline of 20 August to redirect the listed sites to ADM's notice page, and the order supplements rather than replaces the list published on 10 July. The new list includes fonbet-italy.com, fonbet001.com and fonbet003.com, following an earlier round effective 27 July covering Fonbet.com, Fonbet.info and Fonbetpoker.com.",
    "why": "The mirror-domain pattern here is the whole story: three more Fonbet variants two weeks after the originals were blocked. Administrative blocking without a court ruling is fast, but it is a treadmill, and it tells licensed operators how much of their addressable market is still leaking to sites that can respawn on a new subdomain in days.",
    "expanded": "Blocking runs under Article 102 of Decree-Law 104 of 14 August 2020, converted into Law 126 of 13 October 2020, and the obligation falls on ISPs rather than on the operators behind the domains — which is why enforcement capacity, not legal authority, is the binding constraint. Italy is pairing this with the SOGEI \"protective shield\" work and the new complaints portal, so the direction is a more instrumented regulator on both the consumer-facing and infrastructure sides.",
