    "title": "Ukraine study puts online casino channelisation at 86% as PlayCity marks 250 licences",
    "meta": "iGaming Business | 7 Aug 2026",
    "summary": "The second phase of a study commissioned by Ukraine's Ministry of Digital Transformation, conducted by the SOCIOINFORM Sociological Centre between 19 May and 26 June 2026, surveyed 2,676 online casino users and found 86% prefer licensed operators and 78% have no intention of switching to unlicensed sites. Where players are drawn to the black market, the pull factors are quick registration without identity checks (33%), anonymity (17%) and the absence of restrictions or limits (16%). Regulator PlayCity has issued 250 licences in its first year.",
    "why": "The reasons players give for going offshore are all account-journey design problems, not price problems — registration friction, identity verification and limit enforcement. That is an unusually direct piece of evidence that onboarding UX is a channelisation lever, and it is measurable.",
