    "summary": "From Wednesday 12 August 2026, Colorado bettors can no longer fund sports betting apps with credit cards, and deposits are capped at six per player on a rolling 24-hour basis. The rules stem from bipartisan Senate Bill 26-131, passed by the Colorado General Assembly in May 2026 amid growing concern about gambling addiction, particularly among young men. Sponsors say the guardrails are designed to slow down bettors who wager frequently while chasing losses, and sportsbooks began notifying Colorado customers of the changes in early August.",
